From 200145bd465ab734b7e52f8a3f72676c1a9002c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:48:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): adopt local decision ownership from interactive
 chats [daveey]

Timer-filed cards can have observer subscriptions but no chat responsible for
spend decisions. Recommending notify-subscribe leaves them ownerless and creates
another paid supervisor card at every spend stop.

Add origin-adopt TASK --local, using only the current session with fresh local
interactive provenance. Refuse worker/delegated/machine/unknown contexts and
conflicting existing ownership inside the write transaction. Upgrade the exact
observer row to origin without changing card state, routing or notify cursors.
Name this owning path in courier-only tool refusal guidance.

Proof: 11 behavioral tests RED on baseline, then GREEN; expanded local suite
18 passing. 37 import-consumer files: 896 passed, 5 skipped; final changed-owner
and local suites: 54 passed. scripts/check: all 21 checks passed.
